        "topic": "Bank Reconciliation",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2018",
        "question_text": "<p>The cash book balance of a business is \u20b512,000 (Dr). The bank statement shows a balance of \u20b510,500 (Cr). Unpresented cheques amount to \u20b52,000, and bank lodgments not yet credited amount to \u20b5500. What is the adjusted cash book balance?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>To reconcile the cash book balance to the bank statement:<br>1. Start with the cash book balance: \u20b512,000 (Dr).<br>2. Deduct unpresented cheques: \u20b512,000 - \u20b52,000 = \u20b510,000.<br>3. Add lodgments not yet credited: \u20b510,000 + \u20b5500 = <b>\u20b510,500</b>.<br>The adjusted cash book balance matches the bank statement balance.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
